.\" Manual page for ocr_gen
.\" Generated for the OCR-AI C++17 project
.TH OCR_GEN 1 "2026-11-03" "OCR-AI" "User commands"
.SH NAME
ocr_gen - synthetic OCR training data generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
./ocr_gen \-\-fonts DIR \-\-out DIR \-\-count N \-\-shard-size N \-\-seed N \-\-quiet
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generates a synthetic OCR dataset consisting of `.ocrb` shards, a manifest, and
optional sample dumps. All text, backgrounds, and degradations are produced
procedurally in C++17 with no Python dependency.
.PP
The tool supports three text modes (\-\-mode), augmentation profiles
(\-\-augment), and font/background filtering. Output shards follow the OCRB
binary format documented in `FORMAT.md`.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\- fonts DIR
    Directory tree scanned for .ttf/.otf fonts (required).
.PP
\- backgrounds DIR
    Optional directory of PNG/JPEG images used as backgrounds (stb_image decode).
.PP
\- out DIR
    Output directory for shards and manifest.json.
.PP
\- count N
    Number of images to generate (default: 10000).
.PP
\- shard-size N
    Records per shard (default: 10000).
.PP
\- seed N
    Master seed for deterministic generation (default: 1234). Per-record seeds
    are derived as deriveSeed(master_seed, record_index).
.PP
\- width N \- height N
    Image geometry (default: 128x32).
.PP
\- channels N
    1 = grayscale, 3 = RGB (default: 1).
.PP
\- charset STR
    Character set for \-\-mode random-char.
.PP
\- mode MODE
    Text generation mode: random-char | words | numeric.
.PP
\- wordlist FILE
    Path to a word list (required with \-\-mode words).
.PP
\- len-min N \- len-max N
    Label length range (default: 3..20).
.PP
\- size-min N \- size-max N
    Font pixel size range (default: 20..48).
.PP
\- threads N
    Worker threads (default: hardware_concurrency).
.PP
\- augment PROFILE
    Augmentation intensity: full (default) | light | none.
.PP
\- quiet
    Suppress per-image progress output.
.PP
Verification options:
.PP
\- verify DIR
    Validate shards in DIR (structure, checksums).
.PP
\- dump DIR
    Write sample images as .pnm next to labels.txt.
.PP
\- verify-count N
    Number of samples to dump (default: 50).
.SH SHARD FORMAT
All integers little-endian.
.nf
file   := "OCRB" | version:u32 | num_records:u32 | record{num_records}
record := label_len:u32 | label:u8[label_len]
        | h:u32 | w:u32 | ch:u32 | pixels:u8[h*w*ch]
.fi
.PP
version is always 1. The manifest.json alongside the shard records count,
bytes, and SHA-256 per shard.
.SH REPRODUCIBILITY
The same (seed, options) pair always produces byte-identical shards, regardless
of thread count, because each record is seeded via deriveSeed(master_seed,
record_index) and records are reordered by index before writing.
.SH SEE ALSO
FORMAT.md, BENCHMARKS.md, README.md
.SH AUTHOR
Built with NeoML and vendored FreeType. No Python involved.